[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3621062627","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113689#issuecomment-3621062627","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113689","id":3621062627,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7X1Qfj","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-06T19:57:51Z","updated_at":"2025-12-06T19:57:51Z","body":"C# API for Godot Objects is generated from ClassDB, so if these methods are exposed to GDScript they should also be exposed to C#. And, as expected, I was able to confirm the 2 methods you mentioned are exposed to C# in the `FontFile` type:\n\n- `void SetGlyphUVRect(int cacheIndex, Vector2I size, int glyph, Rect2 uVRect)`\n- `void SetGlyphAdvance(int cacheIndex, int size, int glyph, Vector2 advance)`\n\nPlease, double check that the instance you are calling these methods on is of the right type and you are not making any typos. This is why we ask users to provide an MRP, often this helps users find out if they made a mistake or is a real Godot issue.","author_associ